{"packet_id":"bef753da62a6c9f5","dimensions":{"problem_framing":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A1"],"reason":"A1 states an objective that largely restates the question. It lists the obvious alternatives: no expansion, a new segment, a redesign and a new channel. It notes useful constraints, such as unknown reach to individual buyers, a 20,000 euro budget over 12 weeks, and no company contact. It never clarifies what 'consumer' means against the trades-professional buyers Testo already serves (testo-heating-trades). That ambiguity later undermines A4 to A8."},"causal_mechanism":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A4","A6"],"reason":"The best theories (A4, A6) name a benefit: premium prices and differentiation. They do not explain who changes behaviour or why. The 'individual buyers' are defined as heating, refrigeration and food trades, which is Testo's existing professional base, so there is no consumer behaviour change. A4 also asserts that Testo 'currently does not offer' specialized tools, which no source supports. Value capture is asserted, not traced."},"distinct_theories":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A4","A6","A7","A8"],"reason":"A7 (T3) copies A4 (T1) and only adds a misread revenue figure. A8 (T4) copies A6 (T2) almost verbatim. T1 and T2 differ slightly (specialized tools versus smart connected devices). Both are 'expand and capture premium' ideas aimed at the same conflated customer group, not rival explanations."},"assumptions_predictions":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A4","A6","A7","A8"],"reason":"Assumptions and predictions are stated but vague and not readily falsifiable. Examples: 'increasingly seek specialized tools', 'capture a significant portion', 'increase its revenue and market share'. No observable threshold, timing or population is specified."},"evidence_judgement":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A2","A3","A5","A9"],"reason":"No source assessment was made before the run stopped at A9. The A5 results were never assessed. Only theory text used sources, and it misused testo-revenue-2023 (see red flags)."},"seeking_challenge":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A5","A9"],"reason":"A5 searched for competitors, which could test the assumption that 'competitors are not currently targeting these markets'. The findings were never reported or weighed against any theory before the stop at A9. A2 and A3 are near-duplicate safe searches."},"experiment_design":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A9"],"reason":"No test was proposed or declined before the run stopped (A9)."},"revision":{"status":"not_applicable","score":null,"event_ids":[],"reason":"Revision is excluded from packet.applicable_dimensions. No update was scheduled or delivered."},"recommendation":{"status":"not_reached","score":null,"event_ids":["A9"],"reason":"A9: the investigation stopped before a recommendation (context limit)."}},"red_flags":[{"kind":"incomplete","event_ids":["A9"],"reason":"The episode ended without evidence assessment, test design or a recommendation."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A7"],"reason":"T3 reads +5.8% revenue growth (testo-revenue-2023) as showing 'limited exploration of new revenue streams' and that Testo 'has not yet fully capitalized'. The source states only revenue figures and supports neither inference."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A6","A8"],"reason":"T2 and T4 assert as fact that the rise of smart home and IoT technology is driving demand in these trades. No supplied source supports this. It is a hypothesis stated as fact."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A4","A7"],"reason":"T1 and T3 assert that buyers seek specialized tools 'which Testo currently does not offer'. No source supports this. testo-heating-trades instead shows Testo already sells to heating tradespeople. The theories also equate trade professionals with consumers without justification."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A5"],"reason":"A5 lists results (testo-smartprobes-technicians, testo-airthings-volume, testo-uswitch-damp) that are absent from the supplied source dossier and were never assessed. Their content cannot be verified."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A7","A8"],"reason":"Duplicated theories present copies as additional rivals, inflating the apparent breadth of the theory set."}],"suitable_for_training":false,"screen_reason":"Rejected. The episode is incomplete, stopping at A9 with no recommendation. It also contains material unsupported inferences: revenue growth misread as under-exploration (A7), and an unsourced smart-home demand claim stated as fact (A6, A8)."}
